   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the penal law, in relation to crimes involving the death or\nserious physical injury of an employee; and to amend a chapter of the laws of\n2022 amending the penal law relating to crimes involving the death or injury\nof a worker, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S. 621-B and A. 4947-B,\nin relation to the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S1325",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S1325-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§10.00, 20.20, 60.27 & 80.10, Pen L; amd §5, Chap of 2022 (as proposed in S.621-B & A.4947-B)",
    "lawSection": "Penal Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S1325\n\nSPONSOR: SANDERS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the penal law, in relation to crimes involving the death\nor serious physical injury of an employee; and to amend a chapter of the\nlaws of 2022 amending the penal law relating to crimes involving the\ndeath or injury of a worker, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S.\n621-B and A. 4947-B, in relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the penal law, in relation to crimes involving the death\nor serious physical injury of an employee; and to amend a chapter of the\nlaws of 2022 amending the penal law relating to crimes involving the\ndeath or injury of a worker, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S.\n621-B and A. 4947-B, in relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2022,\nc.746, to clarify provisions relating to the applicability of the under-\nlying legislation and its effective date.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation clarifies the persons to whom this bill applies and\nprovides a definition of the term \"employee\" for the purposes of this\nlegislation. The bill clarifies the intent and level of injury required\nfor criminal liability under this legislation. The bill amends the fine\nschedule for criminal liability. This bill amends the effective date of\nthe underlying chapter.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 746 of the Laws of 2022. S-621-A and\nA.4947-B passed the Senate and Assembly, respectively, in June 2021.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided, however, that sections\none, to, three and four of this act shall take effect on the same date\nand in the same manner as a chapter of the laws of 2022 amending the\npenal law relating to crimes involving the death or injury of a worker,\nas proposed in legislative bills numbers S.621-B and A.4947-B, takes\neffect.\n",
